    {
      "id": "note-trigger-rss",
      "name": "note trigger-rss",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        100,
        50
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Declencheur RSS (toutes les 2h)\n\nLit l'onglet `sources` du Google Sheet et filtre sur `is_active=TRUE` et `collection_method=rss`.\nPour chaque source active, n8n itere automatiquement vers RSS Fetch.",
        "height": 130,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-rss-chain",
      "name": "note rss-chain",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        860,
        50
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Chaine RSS\n\n`RSS Fetch` lit le flux, `Attach source_id` rajoute les metadonnees de la source,\n`Normalize RSS` produit un objet standard : title_raw, excerpt_raw, canonical_url (UTM strippes),\nsource_published_at, hash_raw = empreinte unique du titre+URL.",
        "height": 130,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-trigger-gmail",
      "name": "note trigger-gmail",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        100,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Declencheur Gmail (toutes les heures)\n\nPolling du label `📰 Newsletters`. Chaque email recu = un raw_item.\n`Normalize email` extrait From/Subject/body, met source_id=SRC-004, hash_raw=sha du message_id.\nLa date de reception utilise `internalDate` (plus fiable que le header Date).",
        "height": 130,
        "width": 840,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-dedup",
      "name": "note dedup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1540,
        250
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Construction ID stable\n\n`Merge` fusionne les 2 branches (RSS + Email).\n`Build raw_id` genere un ID unique : RAW-AAAAMMJJ-index-hash6.\n\nPas de dedup a ce niveau (volontaire) : la dedup editoriale se fait via `cluster_key` dans canonical_items.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-llm-score",
      "name": "note llm-score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2400,
        50
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Extraction LLM + scoring editorial\n\n`Append raw_items` ecrit l'item brut dans le Sheet.\n`LLM Extract` appelle Claude sur (titre + extrait) -> JSON strict : brand, product, version, event_type, impact_level, key_points, offer.\n`Merge LLM + Raw` rassemble la reponse LLM + les champs Build raw_id (contournement task runner).\n`Parse LLM + score` calcule 8 sous-scores et un editorial_score total. Statut : candidate (>=65) / backlog (>=50) / rejected.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-cluster-write",
      "name": "note cluster-write",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3380,
        50
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Ecriture canonique\n\n`Append canonical_items` ecrit chaque signal editorial avec tous les scores.\n`Append item_sources` trace la liaison raw<->canonical (role: primary).\n\nNote: dedup par cluster_key se fait en post-traitement via une vue Sheets ou un script de nettoyage hebdo.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
  ],
